# 301 redirect map — old WordPress site → this Eleventy site.
# Source of truth: docs/seo-baseline/REDIRECT_MAP.md. Generated for cutover
# (TODO task 10); keep the two in sync if a rule changes here.
#
# Ordering: exact-path rules first, pattern rules last, so a pattern can
# never shadow a more specific exact match above it.
#
# Two things here were learned from the live server, not from the docs, and
# both look like needless verbosity until you know why:
#
#   Targets are absolute https:// URLs rather than plain paths. TLS is
#   terminated upstream (openresty in front of Apache), so Apache sees a
#   plain-HTTP request and builds relative redirects as "http://…" — sending
#   every redirected visitor to the insecure scheme. Writing the scheme
#   explicitly is what stops that. The usual %{HTTPS}-based fix cannot work
#   here: Apache always sees HTTPS as off behind this proxy, so that rule
#   would redirect forever.
#
#   Rules whose target holds a "#" carry the NE (noescape) flag. Without it
#   mod_rewrite percent-encodes it to %23, and /teachers/%23jure-biechonski
#   is a path that doesn't exist — a 404 on the 32 URLs that carry 64% of
#   the site's organic traffic. The first production deploy did exactly that.

RewriteEngine On

# ── §1 Public pages ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# `/` → `/`, `/schedule/` → `/schedule/`, `/apply/` → `/apply/`: same path
# on both sites, so no rule — nothing to redirect.

RewriteRule ^program/?$ https://transpersonal-training.com/training-overview/ [R=301,L]
RewriteRule ^program-2026/?$ https://transpersonal-training.com/training-overview/ [R=301,L]
RewriteRule ^program-2024/?$ https://transpersonal-training.com/training-overview/ [R=301,L]
RewriteRule ^faculty/?$ https://transpersonal-training.com/teachers/ [R=301,L]
RewriteRule ^information/?$ https://transpersonal-training.com/resources/ [R=301,L]

RewriteRule ^archive-2021/?$ https://transpersonal-training.com/schedule/ [R=301,L]
RewriteRule ^archive-2022/?$ https://transpersonal-training.com/schedule/ [R=301,L]
RewriteRule ^archive-2023/?$ https://transpersonal-training.com/schedule/ [R=301,L]
RewriteRule ^archive-2024/?$ https://transpersonal-training.com/schedule/ [R=301,L]
RewriteRule ^archive-2025/?$ https://transpersonal-training.com/schedule/ [R=301,L]

RewriteRule ^closed_meeteing_iurii_becioski-7-9-04-23/?$ - [G,L]

# One old newsletter PDF, marked low-priority in the map with a caution to
# check the GSC Links export for hotlinks first (TODO task 54, still open).
# Gone rather than silently dropped, so a stale hotlink gets a clean 410
# instead of a generic 404.
RewriteRule ^wp-content/uploads/2024/10/newsletter-9\.pdf$ - [G,L]

# `/?page_id=3` — ancient WP-internal query-string URL, path is root.
RewriteCond %{QUERY_STRING} ^page_id=3$
RewriteRule ^$ - [G,L]

# The West Program 2026 PDF was never a separate file — same generator as
# the Curriculum PDF (Fabio, Sep 2026): a Google Apps Script pulls it from
# the spreadsheet on demand (docs/googlescripts/curriculum-pdf-download-apps-script.js).
# That script resolves to a Drive URL at build time (src/_data/curriculumData.js),
# which is why these point at the /curriculum/ page and its live "Download PDF"
# button rather than at a hardcoded Drive link — the Drive URL isn't stable
# enough to bake into .htaccess, the page always has the current one.
RewriteRule ^wp-content/uploads/2025/09/West_Program_26\.pdf$ https://transpersonal-training.com/curriculum/ [R=301,L]
RewriteRule ^wp-content/uploads/2025/10/West_Program_26\.pdf$ https://transpersonal-training.com/curriculum/ [R=301,L]

# ── §2 Teacher bio pages ─────────────────────────────────────────
# 64% of the old site's organic clicks. All 32 consolidate onto the single
# /teachers/ page, which server-renders every bio — see REDIRECT_MAP.md §2
# for why that makes the many-to-one redirect defensible. Each card carries
# id="{{ teacher.id }}" (src/teachers.html), so the fragment opens the right
# bio on arrival.
#
# 28 of 32 old slugs match the teacher's id exactly:

RewriteRule ^bernadette-blin/?$ https://transpersonal-training.com/teachers/#bernadette-blin [R=301,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^dennis-johnson/?$ https://transpersonal-training.com/teachers/#dennis-johnson [R=301,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^kati-wortelkamp/?$ https://transpersonal-training.com/teachers/#kati-wortelkamp [R=301,NE,L]
